---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Gallery" description="See real Chudware modeling, manufacturing, and onboarding workspaces captured from the product.">
  <header class="page-hero gallery-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Product gallery</p><h1>Actual product. No concept renders.</h1><p class="lede">Every image below comes from Chudware itself. They show the current interface and scenario-driven product states rather than composited marketing mockups.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap gallery-grid">
      <figure class="gallery-card gallery-card-wide"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware parametric modeling workspace: a solid part in the 3D view with its ordered construction history in the Feature Manager" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Model</p><h2>Modeling workspace</h2><p>Every feature that built the part stays listed in order beside it, each one still open to being re-dimensioned or reordered.</p></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="gallery-card"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/cam.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace: the machining job tree with stock and tool setup and toolpath simulation controls" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Manufacture</p><h2>CAM workspace</h2><p>Stock, tools, operations, simulation, and post-processing live in the same document as the design they came from.</p></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="gallery-card"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/fea.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware Simulate workspace: a von Mises stress colour map across a loaded part with its scale bar, beside peak stress, displacement, factor of safety, and mesh counts" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Simulate</p><h2>Static stress study</h2><p>Peak stresses, displacement, factor of safety, and the mesh and solver counts that produced them &mdash; reported together. <a class="text-link" href="/product/simulation/">How simulation works</a></p></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="gallery-card"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/onboarding.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware onboarding screen for choosing a starting engineering workspace" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Start</p><h2>Workspace onboarding</h2><p>Open into model, drawing, simulation, electronics, manufacture, PLM, parts library, AI, reverse engineering, or firmware.</p></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
